# Secrets — never commit
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials

# Terraform
.terraform/
# .terraform.lock.hcl is deliberately NOT ignored. It was, until Phase 8 Stage 0, and that was a
# reproducibility defect rather than a style choice: the provider constraint is `~> 6.0`, so a rebuild
# without the lock file is free to resolve a different 6.x than the one every result in this project was
# produced against. Phase 8 criterion 5 is "`make deploy` rebuilds everything destroyed, from clean, in
# one command" -- "from clean" and "unpinned dependencies" cannot both be true. Terraform's own `init`
# output says to commit it.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
terraform.tfvars
!terraform.tfvars.example

